.TH WOWUP-CF-INSTALLER 1 "September 2026" "wowup-cf-installer 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
wowup-cf-installer \- verified official WoWUp CurseForge application delivery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wowup-cf-installer prepare --directory
.I DIR
.RB [ --app-version " VERSION"]
.br
.B wowup-cf-installer apply --appimage
.I PATH
.B --sha256
.I HEX
.B --app-version
.I VERSION
.B --assumeyes
.br
.B wowup-cf-installer status --json
.br
.B wowup-cf-installer uninstall --assumeyes
.br
.B wowup-cf-installer --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
This helper targets Fedora 44 x86_64. The helper RPM contains no application
payload. Installing, upgrading or removing the RPM does not implicitly download,
update or remove the application. DNF updates the helper; application updates
require explicit preparation and approved application of the chosen artifact.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B prepare
Run without root. Download the latest stable official CurseForge AppImage, or
the version selected with --app-version, into a private child of an existing
directory. Verify its exact HTTPS release URL, GitHub SHA-256, expected size and
x86_64 type-2 AppImage identity. Print metadata JSON with schema_version, name,
arch, version, sha256, path and source. The caller owns successful-download
cleanup and must show the selected artifact before approval. Failure removes
the incomplete download. These checks are not a publisher signature.
.TP
.B apply
Require root and --assumeyes. Work offline. Copy the selected artifact into
private privileged staging, verify it again, refuse downgrades and extract
with native unsquashfs without executing the downloaded runtime. Verify owned
files before replacement. Publish the bundle and install the fixed integration
links. Print verified installed-state JSON. The caller must approve the exact
version and SHA-256 before invoking this command.
.TP
.B status
Read-only and offline. Print JSON containing schema_version, name, installed,
verified, integrated and cleanup_pending, plus the approved identity when
installed. Invalid or foreign state is an error, never successful absence.
Missing known integration links are repairable through approved apply.
.TP
.B uninstall
Require root and --assumeyes. Verify ownership before removing integration
links and the application bundle. A durable removal journal permits resuming
interrupted removal. Foreign or modified surviving entries block cleanup.
Preserve home directories, application settings, games and addons.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/wowup-cf/
Owned AppImage, extracted app, launcher, desktop entry and inventory receipt.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/wowup-cf
Owned symlink to the launch wrapper.
.TP
.B /usr/local/share/applications/wowup-cf.desktop
Owned symlink to the desktop entry.
.TP
.B /opt/.nimbus-wowup-cf-removal.json
Durable ownership journal for interrupted removal.
.TP
.B /opt/.nimbus-wowup-cf-removing
Owned pending-removal bundle. These established paths retain their original
Nimbus names for lifecycle compatibility.
.SH NOTES
The launcher clears AppImage updater environment variables, preserving addon
updates and Chromium sandboxing. There is no timer, daemon or background update
service. Bundle exchange is atomic; the complete install or removal transaction
is not. Missing known links and interrupted removal can be retried, while
unknown ownership or modified files require inspection. Empty parent directories
remain after removal. Remove the application explicitly before removing its
helper if both should be removed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Nonzero indicates invalid input, unsupported platform,
unverified ownership or a failed operation. SIGTERM and keyboard interruption
return nonzero. A failed operation must not receive a successful caller receipt.
